# M-inferred-cell step 1, panel 209's R1b (spec § 5): a cell nothing
# re-binds is a binding written with the wrong symbol. The one message
# stands at the cell's name, and its certain fix writes `=` where the `@`
# is, the annotation kept; the program then means what it meant, since
# nothing ever wrote the cell. Measured on the tree the day the rule
# landed: 156 such cells in the compiler, 18 in the examples, 5 in the
# harness, 212 in the goldens, every one read a `=` in disguise.
function main()
    v: i64 @= 5           #~ never_rebound
    print(v)
